1
00:00:08,940 --> 00:00:13,380
Brighten up the peace, then step away, okay?

2
00:00:24,220 --> 00:00:27,000
Hello, goodbye.

3
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:31,500
Someone who heads straight
home once their errand is done.

4
00:00:32,400 --> 00:00:35,360
Wappara puwa, wappara

5
00:00:36,960 --> 00:00:39,980
Wappara buwa chi wappara

6
00:00:40,840 --> 00:00:45,560
Don't rush, in this narrow town,

7
00:00:45,560 --> 00:00:49,400
where are you going? Haste makes waste,
so take the long way round.

8
00:00:49,920 --> 00:00:58,540
If, by any chance,
there's someone better than me,

9
00:00:59,340 --> 00:01:03,020
tell me, tell me all through the night.

10
00:01:08,420 --> 00:01:12,820
I don't mind waiting at all.

11
00:01:12,820 --> 00:01:17,020
Because I'm a Kame-za woman.

12
00:01:17,900 --> 00:01:21,720
I won't lose to a Ginza woman.

13
00:01:21,720 --> 00:01:26,520
I'll love you for years and years.

14
00:01:27,140 --> 00:01:29,840
The everyday life of a Kame-za woman.

15
00:01:44,660 --> 00:01:46,420
- He's going!
- Abera! Help me!

16
00:01:46,580 --> 00:01:48,280
- Go!
- Go!

17
00:01:48,360 --> 00:01:49,960
- Go!
- Go!

18
00:01:49,960 --> 00:01:53,100
- Go!
- Go!

19
00:01:53,100 --> 00:01:53,360
- Go!
- Go!

20
00:01:53,360 --> 00:01:54,060
- Go!
- Go!

21
00:01:54,320 --> 00:02:04,513
Go!

22
00:02:04,563 --> 00:02:13,100
Go!

23
00:02:14,660 --> 00:02:15,640
Then stick out your tongue.

24
00:02:17,620 --> 00:02:19,780
Look, my tongue is green!

25
00:02:20,160 --> 00:02:21,440
You idiot!

26
00:02:21,860 --> 00:02:23,440
Get serious and do your job.

27
00:02:23,440 --> 00:02:26,780
The tsukkomi keeps
getting harsher day by day.

28
00:02:27,160 --> 00:02:29,700
Senpai, your green is way too conspicuous.

29
00:02:29,700 --> 00:02:31,200
What's with you anyway?

30
00:02:31,200 --> 00:02:33,980
We all ate shaved ice together just now,
didn't we?

31
00:02:35,200 --> 00:02:37,420
Reiko, stick out your tongue!

32
00:02:38,920 --> 00:02:40,240
It's not colored.

33
00:02:40,660 --> 00:02:43,060
We ate strawberry shaved ice, after all.

34
00:02:44,980 --> 00:02:46,820
Gross, you two are the only ones.

35
00:02:47,560 --> 00:02:50,860
But Ryo-chan,
why do you always eat melon shaved ice?

36
00:02:51,060 --> 00:02:54,339
Is that so? It's melon in name only,

37
00:02:54,389 --> 00:02:57,220
it doesn't contain any melon juice at all.

38
00:02:57,240 --> 00:02:58,687
I was poor since I was little,

39
00:02:58,737 --> 00:03:01,882
and I was conditioned to believe
melon was expensive and luxurious,

40
00:03:01,932 --> 00:03:03,900
so I just can't resist being drawn to melon.

41
00:03:04,040 --> 00:03:04,840
Is that right?

42
00:03:05,060 --> 00:03:06,241
Yeah.

43
00:03:06,291 --> 00:03:09,780
Poverty has seeped into
my bones and won't let go.

44
00:03:10,800 --> 00:03:16,380
When I was a kid eating ice at the candy store,
I always got the cheapest kind, plain ice water.

45
00:03:16,380 --> 00:03:18,100
What's ice water?

46
00:03:18,100 --> 00:03:22,240
It's sugar-water syrup,
the kind with no color at all.

47
00:03:22,700 --> 00:03:24,200
Did that really exist?

48
00:03:24,200 --> 00:03:26,680
Sugar water,
that's like something for stag beetles.

49
00:03:26,680 --> 00:03:28,700
What a rough era that was.

50
00:03:28,700 --> 00:03:32,660
That's why I always end
up eating melon shaved ice.

51
00:03:33,300 --> 00:03:36,100
It's all because of my poverty.

52
00:03:36,100 --> 00:03:39,700
I wish a pile of money would
just fall from somewhere.

53
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:44,400
What, a treasure worth 20 billion yen?

54
00:03:44,400 --> 00:03:49,540
So a Edo-period vermilion-seal
ship carrying gold bullion sank?

55
00:03:49,540 --> 00:03:53,580
Recently they found where it sank,
off the Ogasawara coast.

56
00:03:53,580 --> 00:03:56,960
Something about this really stirs the imagination,
doesn't it?

57
00:03:56,960 --> 00:04:00,640
Yeah, it's romantic, sunk ten
thousand meters down in the deep sea.

58
00:04:00,640 --> 00:04:02,220
Twenty billion yen

59
00:04:02,220 --> 00:04:04,700
Damn it, and whoever gets there first wins!

60
00:04:04,700 --> 00:04:08,420
Ten thousand meters under the sea,
we can't lay a finger on it!

61
00:04:08,420 --> 00:04:10,800
Eee-yo!

62
00:04:11,660 --> 00:04:15,640
No way, no way, no way!

63
00:04:15,640 --> 00:04:17,540
No way, no way, no way!

64
00:04:18,500 --> 00:04:19,300
W-what's this?

65
00:04:21,840 --> 00:04:22,940
Haaah.

66
00:04:22,940 --> 00:04:24,120
Hahaha!

67
00:04:24,640 --> 00:04:26,860
Gentlemen, the sea is wonderful.

68
00:04:26,860 --> 00:04:28,020
It's magnificent!

69
00:04:30,640 --> 00:04:32,080
Just as I thought, it's you!
Some professor you are!

70
00:04:32,540 --> 00:04:34,520
You run on wheels,
so don't go running aground!

71
00:04:34,640 --> 00:04:36,720
Where in Kameari is there any sea, anyway?

72
00:04:36,900 --> 00:04:40,580
Gorilla-kun,
the sea is the source of all life.

73
00:04:40,580 --> 00:04:42,880
Even if there's no sea before our eyes,

74
00:04:42,880 --> 00:04:46,020
if I close my eyes like this,
I can hear the sound of the surf.

75
00:04:46,900 --> 00:04:49,380
The sea is truly the homeland of mankind.

76
00:04:49,380 --> 00:04:53,800
Looks like you've done every country in the world,
and now you've gone crazy over the sea.

77
00:04:53,800 --> 00:04:55,180
Looks like it, doesn't it.

78
00:04:56,960 --> 00:04:59,000
Oh no, we can't have that! It's tea time!

79
00:05:03,080 --> 00:05:06,360
A sea man's drink is kombu tea,
no question about it.

80
00:05:06,360 --> 00:05:09,220
Why is kombu tea a sea man's drink?

81
00:05:09,220 --> 00:05:10,120
Well,

82
00:05:11,480 --> 00:05:13,300
so here's a question for you, Gorilla-kun.

83
00:05:13,780 --> 00:05:17,240
What percentage of the Earth's total
surface area does the sea make up?

84
00:05:17,240 --> 00:05:21,140
What does that loincloth getup
have to do with this question?

85
00:05:21,960 --> 00:05:25,460
I think it's about 70% sea, right?

86
00:05:25,900 --> 00:05:27,580
As expected of Nakagawa-kun.

87
00:05:27,580 --> 00:05:32,640
To be precise,
it's 70.8%. The sea is 2.42 times the land.

88
00:05:32,640 --> 00:05:34,280
So what?

89
00:05:34,280 --> 00:05:36,120
So what, you punk?

90
00:05:36,120 --> 00:05:40,860
A sea man has to understand
the sea inside and out.

91
00:05:41,280 --> 00:05:45,320
The flat seabed surrounding the land, stretching
from the coast out toward the open sea,

92
00:05:45,320 --> 00:05:49,040
what do you call the part up to the edge where
it suddenly drops off into the deep seabed?

93
00:05:49,540 --> 00:05:51,600
The continental shelf,
the continental shelf!

94
00:05:51,600 --> 00:05:53,300
Then what's this, then?

95
00:05:53,720 --> 00:05:55,100
Hey, don't you go peeking
at your cheat sheet!

96
00:05:59,120 --> 00:06:02,460
Anyway,
we can't win our future without invention.

97
00:06:02,460 --> 00:06:04,500
Aren't you overdoing it a bit?

98
00:06:04,500 --> 00:06:06,040
So then, Gorilla-kun.

99
00:06:06,040 --> 00:06:09,540
We're going to need your
off-the-charts vitality.

100
00:06:09,540 --> 00:06:10,800
What are you talking about?

101
00:06:10,800 --> 00:06:12,700
Looks like you've finally
gotten to the main point.

102
00:06:12,700 --> 00:06:14,080
Let me just come out and say it.

103
00:06:14,080 --> 00:06:17,040
Professor Korosuke Ezaki invented this

104
00:06:17,040 --> 00:06:21,100
deep-sea suit, and I'll give you the
honor of being the first to wear it.

105
00:06:21,100 --> 00:06:22,580
Deep-sea suit?

106
00:06:23,020 --> 00:06:23,820
That's right.

107
00:06:25,100 --> 00:06:30,280
With this body suit, you can move freely on the seabed,
even beyond 10,000 meters.

108
00:06:30,280 --> 00:06:37,000
Be overjoyed, because your name will go down
in history as Mister Kankichi Gorilla Ryotsu.

109
00:06:37,000 --> 00:06:41,600
Stop with the
"Gorilla" middle name! No way, I refuse.

110
00:06:41,600 --> 00:06:48,060
Do you have any idea how many times your inventions have put me through hell?
I've had enough, and I'm not doing it.

111
00:06:48,060 --> 00:06:51,600
Gorilla-kun, you're being so pushy,
joking around like that!

112
00:06:52,320 --> 00:06:55,540
Come on, let's go! Let's go to the sea!

113
00:06:55,540 --> 00:06:58,980
I already told you I don't want to!
You're impossible to understand.

114
00:06:58,980 --> 00:07:04,420
Wait, if that deep-sea
suit actually existed...

115
00:07:07,440 --> 00:07:11,060
I see... Alright, I'm in on this.

116
00:07:22,500 --> 00:07:23,980
The sea is nice, isn't it?

117
00:07:23,980 --> 00:07:26,020
I'm so glad I decided to take some time off.

118
00:07:26,020 --> 00:07:28,600
I suppose the Chief and
Tora-san have it rough, though.

119
00:07:28,600 --> 00:07:30,260
Who cares!

120
00:07:30,260 --> 00:07:33,380
When we get back,
we'll be filthy rich with 20 billion yen!

121
00:07:33,780 --> 00:07:34,860
I'll have you know,

122
00:07:34,860 --> 00:07:36,800
I'm the one who's going
to risk my neck to get it.

123
00:07:36,800 --> 00:07:38,800
You two aren't getting a single question!

124
00:07:38,800 --> 00:07:40,780
Honestly, once Ryo-chan gets involved,

125
00:07:40,780 --> 00:07:43,160
the romance of the sea turns
into a way to make money.

126
00:07:43,660 --> 00:07:45,740
Don't worry,
we're not going to take it from you.

127
00:07:45,740 --> 00:07:48,740
Says the one who's secretly expecting a lot!

128
00:07:50,540 --> 00:07:54,220
Sea, vast sea that stretches on forever,

129
00:07:54,220 --> 00:07:59,720
after all, the sea is my hometown.
Isn't it wonderful?

130
00:07:59,720 --> 00:08:01,600
Hey, Aodaisho-kun.

131
00:08:02,060 --> 00:08:03,260
Aodaisho

132
00:08:03,880 --> 00:08:06,840
I was going for the Wakadaisho
series with Yuzo Kayama.

133
00:08:06,840 --> 00:08:10,720
The rival Aodaisho was played by Kunie Tanaka in
"From the Land of the North."

134
00:08:10,720 --> 00:08:14,100
I thought you meant Shinji Maki,
the ukulele comedian.

135
00:08:15,740 --> 00:08:17,320
It doesn't feel like a Wakadaisho at all.

136
00:08:17,660 --> 00:08:19,400
Well then, let's do this.

137
00:08:19,400 --> 00:08:21,800
He's a gorilla from the sea,
so he's Umi-Gorilla-kun.

138
00:08:21,800 --> 00:08:22,160
Hey!

139
00:08:22,760 --> 00:08:25,280
You have no naming sense whatsoever!

140
00:08:26,420 --> 00:08:27,740
Well, it's tea time.

141
00:08:28,542 --> 00:08:33,560
a sea Wakadaisho really
suits tropical drinks.

142
00:08:34,860 --> 00:08:37,100
Weren't men of the sea
supposed to drink kelp tea?

143
00:08:37,880 --> 00:08:40,640
Anyway, senpai,
we're about to hit the sinking point.

144
00:08:45,900 --> 00:08:48,620
Looks like we're the first ones here.

145
00:08:48,620 --> 00:08:50,800
As expected of Nakagawa's express line.

146
00:08:50,800 --> 00:08:52,180
Hey, no way!

147
00:08:53,460 --> 00:08:56,240
Hey, Ezaki, Ezaki, shall we kill him?

148
00:08:57,840 --> 00:09:02,360
Don't we have to call out to him as
"Aodaisho," or something?

149
00:09:02,360 --> 00:09:04,900
What a troublesome guy.

150
00:09:05,340 --> 00:09:07,440
He's really gotten into the role, hasn't he.

151
00:09:07,820 --> 00:09:08,660
There's no helping it.

152
00:09:11,480 --> 00:09:13,800
Have you read it, Umigurera-kun?

153
00:09:13,800 --> 00:09:15,420
Yeah, as I thought.

154
00:09:15,420 --> 00:09:19,200
Senpai says he wants to
start the suit experiment soon.

155
00:09:19,200 --> 00:09:22,140
I was just thinking the same thing.

156
00:09:22,140 --> 00:09:23,680
Let's start the experiment right away!

157
00:09:25,940 --> 00:09:28,580
This is the deep-sea suit I invented.

158
00:09:28,580 --> 00:09:31,400
It's called the 8823-15.

159
00:09:31,400 --> 00:09:33,060
That's just a suit, isn't it?

160
00:09:33,060 --> 00:09:35,800
Do I look like a waiter
at the Dragon Palace?

161
00:09:35,800 --> 00:09:36,880
Don't worry.

162
00:09:36,880 --> 00:09:40,900
The fabric of this suit is waterproofed,
so it'll keep you safe in any downpour.

163
00:09:40,900 --> 00:09:42,760
There's no way you can dive in that.

164
00:09:43,940 --> 00:09:45,480
Just kidding, it's a joke.

165
00:09:45,480 --> 00:09:48,440
Honestly,
I can never tell how serious you are.

166
00:09:49,580 --> 00:09:50,680
Well then, once more.

167
00:09:51,840 --> 00:09:56,240
This is the deep-sea suit I invented,
model 8823-2.

168
00:09:57,000 --> 00:09:58,420
It looks like a snowman.

169
00:09:58,800 --> 00:10:02,580
Underwater, the pressure increases by about one atmosphere
every 10 meters you descend.

170
00:10:02,980 --> 00:10:05,460
So at 10,000 meters,
it's a thousand atmospheres.

171
00:10:07,080 --> 00:10:09,020
That means a weight of
one ton bears down on it.

172
00:10:09,020 --> 00:10:10,040
One whole ton!

173
00:10:10,040 --> 00:10:15,000
What protects against that water pressure is this deep-sea suit,
model 8823-15.

174
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:18,000
It may look like a snowman,
but its functions are superb.

175
00:10:18,000 --> 00:10:21,380
With this, you'll be safe.
It suits you, Ryo-chan!

176
00:10:21,380 --> 00:10:25,480
As if it would be! But this really
is heavy and hard to move in.

177
00:10:26,400 --> 00:10:27,860
Because it weighs 20 tons.

178
00:10:27,860 --> 00:10:31,200
Twenty tons?! I'm going to fall over!

179
00:10:32,180 --> 00:10:35,840
Don't worry. It has weights at the bottom,
so it'll never get tangled.

180
00:10:36,880 --> 00:10:38,800
- Interesting!
- Hey, stop it already!

181
00:10:39,200 --> 00:10:40,860
Am I a roly-poly doll?!

182
00:10:41,720 --> 00:10:45,580
Hey, I'm exhausted.
Isn't there something better?

183
00:10:45,720 --> 00:10:49,460
Don't worry. This time,
I've definitely got an ace up my sleeve.

184
00:10:49,680 --> 00:10:52,760
It's the deep-sea suit, model 8823-15!

185
00:10:54,760 --> 00:10:56,640
It's, it's actually decent!

186
00:10:56,780 --> 00:10:58,340
With this,
it really looks like it could dive.

187
00:10:58,600 --> 00:10:59,000
Of course!

188
00:10:59,300 --> 00:11:00,860
If you've got one,
bring it out of that hole!

189
00:11:02,620 --> 00:11:04,540
This one's good, it moves easily.

190
00:11:04,540 --> 00:11:06,560
It's like a space suit, isn't it?

191
00:11:06,560 --> 00:11:08,840
The unknown deep sea is the same as space.

192
00:11:08,840 --> 00:11:09,980
Truly mysterious.

193
00:11:09,980 --> 00:11:12,340
With this 8823-35,

194
00:11:12,340 --> 00:11:15,780
it's designed to withstand the
water pressure of 10,000 meters.

195
00:11:16,340 --> 00:11:16,960
should be.

196
00:11:16,960 --> 00:11:18,840
Hold on.

197
00:11:18,840 --> 00:11:20,120
What do you mean, "should be"?

198
00:11:20,120 --> 00:11:21,140
"Should be"

199
00:11:21,540 --> 00:11:23,960
You did proper water pressure tests, right?

200
00:11:23,960 --> 00:11:24,980
We tested it in my bath.

201
00:11:26,180 --> 00:11:28,560
Don't compare a bath to 10,000 meters!

202
00:11:28,560 --> 00:11:29,680
Sea Gorilla-kun.

203
00:11:29,680 --> 00:11:32,360
This is no time for such leisurely talk.

204
00:11:32,360 --> 00:11:33,460
Look over there.

205
00:11:38,480 --> 00:11:41,040
It's the ship of the official
survey team from the newspaper.

206
00:11:41,040 --> 00:11:43,440
Damn it,
we can't let them get ahead of us like this!

207
00:11:43,440 --> 00:11:45,180
20 billion yen! 20 billion yen!

208
00:11:52,420 --> 00:11:53,780
Standby, all set.

209
00:11:54,280 --> 00:11:56,640
Alright then, Gorilla-kun, count on you.

210
00:12:02,340 --> 00:12:03,840
Will he be okay, Ryo-chan?

211
00:12:04,660 --> 00:12:09,300
According to the data from the pro tests, it should
be fine even at 20,000 meters, by the calculations.

212
00:12:09,300 --> 00:12:10,120
Really?

213
00:12:10,120 --> 00:12:10,900
It's fine.

214
00:12:10,900 --> 00:12:14,900
Even if something goes wrong,
Gorilla-kun will surely come back alive.

215
00:12:16,880 --> 00:12:18,080
I'm worried.

216
00:12:21,340 --> 00:12:22,140
7500

217
00:12:22,140 --> 00:12:23,400
7800

218
00:12:23,840 --> 00:12:24,640
8000

219
00:12:26,020 --> 00:12:28,320
Hey, it's really going to be all right,
isn't it?

220
00:12:28,320 --> 00:12:31,700
Whoa, it can't be that reckless, can it?

221
00:12:31,700 --> 00:12:32,960
A deep-sea fish

222
00:12:34,540 --> 00:12:36,980
Got a bit of a fright there with the deep-sea fish,
didn't you, Gorilla-kun?

223
00:12:36,980 --> 00:12:38,680
Don't make such lame puns!

224
00:12:38,700 --> 00:12:40,840
Never mind that, the suit's creaking!

225
00:12:41,080 --> 00:12:43,620
Haha, it's fine, probably.

226
00:12:43,620 --> 00:12:45,280
Hey, stop with the "probably"!

227
00:12:46,060 --> 00:12:47,554
Depth: 9,800 meters,

228
00:12:47,604 --> 00:12:51,080
we should be reaching
the seabed soon, senpai.

229
00:12:51,080 --> 00:12:52,800
Ryo-chan, can you see anything?

230
00:12:53,060 --> 00:12:55,540
Nothing yet! Whoa, woo-hoo!

231
00:12:55,600 --> 00:12:56,900
Ryo-chan, what's wrong?

232
00:12:57,520 --> 00:12:59,860
Looks like he's reached the seabed!

233
00:13:00,680 --> 00:13:02,100
Yes, it worked!

234
00:13:02,100 --> 00:13:04,100
Is there any leak anywhere?

235
00:13:04,100 --> 00:13:05,420
Is his heart still beating?

236
00:13:05,420 --> 00:13:06,460
Of course it is.

237
00:13:06,920 --> 00:13:07,940
How about the sunken ship?

238
00:13:07,940 --> 00:13:09,400
Can you see anything around?

239
00:13:09,400 --> 00:13:10,600
The sunken ship

240
00:13:11,840 --> 00:13:12,480
Let's see...

241
00:13:12,880 --> 00:13:13,800
That's odd.

242
00:13:13,800 --> 00:13:16,060
There's nothing that looks like one.

243
00:13:18,200 --> 00:13:18,940
What's wrong?

244
00:13:18,940 --> 00:13:19,680
Senpai!

245
00:13:20,840 --> 00:13:21,480
What is it? What is it?

246
00:13:22,640 --> 00:13:23,920
What on earth is that?

247
00:13:23,920 --> 00:13:25,200
Be careful!

248
00:13:25,200 --> 00:13:27,660
It might be an unknown creature
that lives in the deep sea.

249
00:13:27,660 --> 00:13:29,640
What are we supposed to do
if it's an unknown creature?

250
00:13:29,640 --> 00:13:31,720
Fine, just let it eat
you and be done with it.

251
00:13:31,720 --> 00:13:33,840
That way, we'll know exactly
what kind of creature it is.

252
00:13:33,840 --> 00:13:35,460
Don't joke at a time like this!

253
00:13:36,120 --> 00:13:37,240
It's coming this way!

254
00:13:37,240 --> 00:13:39,780
Stop! I'm not tasty at all!

255
00:13:39,780 --> 00:13:40,860
Don't worry.

256
00:13:40,860 --> 00:13:41,800
D-death, death...

257
00:13:55,460 --> 00:14:03,620
Aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaah!

258
00:14:03,620 --> 00:14:06,580
There are two of these!
Which one is it, red or blue?

259
00:14:08,500 --> 00:14:09,060
Red.

260
00:14:09,060 --> 00:14:10,640
It's red, right? Okay!

261
00:14:11,820 --> 00:14:12,380
Maybe.

262
00:14:12,380 --> 00:14:14,900
Whoa, you idiot! I told you to stop with the
"maybe"!

263
00:14:20,380 --> 00:14:21,100
Whoa.

264
00:14:21,600 --> 00:14:22,400
S-senpai...

265
00:14:22,400 --> 00:14:22,900
Ryo-chan!

266
00:14:22,900 --> 00:14:26,260
What happened to Gorilla-kun?
Respond, Gorilla-kun!

267
00:14:30,660 --> 00:14:31,380
Thank goodness.

268
00:14:32,340 --> 00:14:34,460
Who was it that said "unknown creature"?

269
00:14:34,960 --> 00:14:36,620
It's an unmanned exploration vessel,
isn't it?

270
00:14:37,120 --> 00:14:39,100
But it even has missiles attached!

271
00:14:39,540 --> 00:14:41,760
Looks like you've changed my opinion of you,
Gorilla-kun.

272
00:14:41,760 --> 00:14:44,600
By the way,
the blue button is a self-destruct device.

273
00:14:46,380 --> 00:14:49,280
Who'd be idiot enough to
self-destruct at the bottom of the sea?

274
00:14:54,260 --> 00:14:56,340
Found it! It's the sunken ship!

275
00:14:57,060 --> 00:15:00,540
That explosion just now uncovered what
had been buried in the seabed sand.

276
00:15:01,540 --> 00:15:03,580
Everything went according to plan.
I made it all work out.

277
00:15:03,580 --> 00:15:05,000
We did it, Ryo-chan!

278
00:15:05,000 --> 00:15:07,260
Then let's get right to treasure hunting!

279
00:15:07,260 --> 00:15:07,900
Here we go!

280
00:15:12,980 --> 00:15:17,060
This is what appeared on the unmanned
probe's footage before it cut out.

281
00:15:17,760 --> 00:15:19,480
W-what is this thing?

282
00:15:20,020 --> 00:15:21,700
Th-there's no mistaking it,
it's a living creature.

283
00:15:21,700 --> 00:15:25,140
It also looks like a human or a gorilla.

284
00:15:25,140 --> 00:15:27,740
But this is the deep sea, at 10,000 meters.

285
00:15:27,740 --> 00:15:30,960
This might just be the
discovery of the century.

286
00:15:31,380 --> 00:15:34,180
Let's call this mysterious
creature the Seabed Caveman for now.

287
00:15:34,180 --> 00:15:35,820
We're going to investigate it thoroughly!

288
00:15:35,920 --> 00:15:36,460
Understood.

289
00:15:37,120 --> 00:15:39,760
Alright,
this time we're lowering the manned probe!

290
00:15:39,880 --> 00:15:40,800
I'm going too!

291
00:15:40,900 --> 00:15:41,340
Roger!

292
00:15:50,740 --> 00:15:51,800
No doubt about it!

293
00:15:52,160 --> 00:15:53,760
It's an ancient sunken ship!

294
00:15:54,080 --> 00:15:56,680
Now that 20 billion
yen in gold bars is mine!

295
00:15:57,640 --> 00:15:58,780
Gold bars, gold bars,

296
00:15:58,780 --> 00:16:17,340
Aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaah!

297
00:16:21,100 --> 00:16:23,740
Who asked you to go and find that junk?

298
00:16:23,740 --> 00:16:25,400
Gold bars, I'm telling you, gold bars!

299
00:16:25,400 --> 00:16:28,160
I know that without you telling me.

300
00:16:28,160 --> 00:16:31,680
Where are you, my little gold bars?

301
00:16:31,680 --> 00:16:34,020
That's 20 billion yen, you know!

302
00:16:34,740 --> 00:16:35,140
This is...

303
00:16:41,740 --> 00:16:44,260
Found it! A mountain of gold!

304
00:16:45,280 --> 00:16:46,780
Well done, Gorilla-kun!

305
00:16:48,420 --> 00:16:50,100
We won't be able to
carry it all in one trip.

306
00:16:51,100 --> 00:16:53,120
This is the dream of a true man of the sea!

307
00:16:53,120 --> 00:16:56,220
Quick, cram as much as you can
into the backpack on your back!

308
00:16:56,220 --> 00:16:58,140
Right, the backpack! The backpack!

309
00:17:01,020 --> 00:17:02,800
I can't reach my back!

310
00:17:02,800 --> 00:17:05,320
This thing has a design flaw!

311
00:17:07,080 --> 00:17:08,900
Ow, my arm cramped up!

312
00:17:10,520 --> 00:17:11,600
How pitiful.

313
00:17:14,100 --> 00:17:16,720
Damn it, I thought I'd
finally gotten the backpack off!

314
00:17:18,340 --> 00:17:22,000
Geez! It's so slippery, it's hard to grip!

315
00:17:27,120 --> 00:17:28,860
So this is the sunken ship.

316
00:17:29,280 --> 00:17:31,220
Professor, shall we begin the survey?

317
00:17:31,480 --> 00:17:33,960
The 20 billion yen in
gold isn't going anywhere!

318
00:17:34,160 --> 00:17:35,920
First, the sea-floor primitive man!

319
00:17:36,720 --> 00:17:41,260
If we can capture that sea-floor primitive man alive,
it'll be a discovery that shakes the whole world!

320
00:17:41,260 --> 00:17:43,820
It might even be worthy of a Nobel Prize.

321
00:17:44,540 --> 00:17:45,080
Right!

322
00:17:48,340 --> 00:17:50,040
It's the survey team's new seabed find!

323
00:17:50,040 --> 00:17:52,740
Damn it,
I'm not handing over 20 billion yen!

324
00:17:55,120 --> 00:17:57,360
Where is it, the sea-floor primitive man?

325
00:17:57,360 --> 00:17:59,660
There, there, good boy,
little primitive man.

326
00:18:00,560 --> 00:18:01,820
What is it? What happened?

327
00:18:01,820 --> 00:18:04,760
S-something just latched onto the ship!

328
00:18:04,760 --> 00:18:07,160
N-no way...
could it be the Seabed Primitive Man?

329
00:18:07,160 --> 00:18:09,620
Hah, how about that, you bastard!

330
00:18:15,180 --> 00:18:17,540
Damn, what a ferocious creature!

331
00:18:18,340 --> 00:18:19,180
- Shake it off!
- Roger!

332
00:18:20,400 --> 00:18:21,580
You wanna go, pal!

333
00:18:22,720 --> 00:18:24,400
I'm not going down that easily!

334
00:18:25,320 --> 00:18:27,020
Where is it? Seabed Primitive Man!

335
00:18:29,040 --> 00:18:32,300
No doubt about it! It's the Seabed
Primitive Man! Catch it quick!

336
00:18:32,660 --> 00:18:34,100
Fire the capture wire!

337
00:18:40,440 --> 00:18:41,720
What's this? What are you doing?

338
00:18:43,660 --> 00:18:45,420
Let go! Let go of me!

339
00:18:45,900 --> 00:18:47,380
Oh no! Ryo-chan!

340
00:18:48,380 --> 00:18:49,760
Press the button on the arm.

341
00:18:49,760 --> 00:18:52,140
It's not a self-destruct device, is it?

342
00:18:52,140 --> 00:18:53,260
No, hurry!

343
00:18:53,820 --> 00:18:54,360
This one?

344
00:18:57,180 --> 00:18:57,900
This one is -

345
00:18:58,540 --> 00:18:59,940
a diamond cutter!

346
00:18:59,940 --> 00:19:01,580
A wire like that is nothing.

347
00:19:01,580 --> 00:19:02,660
Alright!

348
00:19:05,560 --> 00:19:07,040
The wire's been cut!

349
00:19:07,040 --> 00:19:08,660
It's no good, it's getting away!

350
00:19:08,660 --> 00:19:11,240
Shit, can't we do something?

351
00:19:11,920 --> 00:19:13,560
What the hell!
You really did it now, you bastard!

352
00:19:13,560 --> 00:19:15,380
Now it's our turn to pay you back!

353
00:19:15,380 --> 00:19:16,580
You bastard!

354
00:19:18,340 --> 00:19:18,840
This is it!

355
00:19:18,840 --> 00:19:19,860
Whoa!

356
00:19:20,120 --> 00:19:22,340
Unfair! Unfair! Hurry!

357
00:19:23,320 --> 00:19:27,220
Take this, you pest!
Spank-spank on the rear, kick-kick!

358
00:19:27,260 --> 00:19:28,780
Get lost, you son of a bitch!

359
00:19:29,900 --> 00:19:30,860
We drove it off.

360
00:19:31,500 --> 00:19:34,380
As expected of you, senpai,
you really go all out!

361
00:19:34,380 --> 00:19:38,200
Then, Sea Gorilla-kun,
grab as much gold as you can carry, hurry!

362
00:19:38,200 --> 00:19:39,400
I know, I know!

363
00:19:40,800 --> 00:19:44,040
Jackpot, jackpot! With this, I'm a rich man!

364
00:19:44,660 --> 00:19:46,650
Money goes around the world,

365
00:19:46,700 --> 00:19:49,420
and with it,
this world is paradise, they say!

366
00:19:50,760 --> 00:19:53,702
Ryo-chan,

367
00:19:53,752 --> 00:19:56,694
something's coming closer,

368
00:19:56,744 --> 00:19:58,240
be careful!

369
00:19:58,240 --> 00:20:00,180
What? Where?

370
00:20:00,180 --> 00:20:01,400
Below you, Ryo-chan!

371
00:20:05,180 --> 00:20:06,980
Get away, you idiot, rat-a-tat!

372
00:20:06,980 --> 00:20:09,900
I'm not tasty, you know.
I haven't had a bath in a week!

373
00:20:12,380 --> 00:20:13,920
You stubborn shark!

374
00:20:13,920 --> 00:20:15,280
I'll take care of you!

375
00:20:21,940 --> 00:20:23,220
This is unbearable!

376
00:20:23,220 --> 00:20:24,920
Hey, hurry up and haul me up!

377
00:20:26,580 --> 00:20:28,280
You really are a handful, aren't you.

378
00:20:28,680 --> 00:20:29,120
This is tough!

379
00:20:36,960 --> 00:20:39,240
Professor, if we don't reel it in faster,

380
00:20:39,900 --> 00:20:41,560
But this is already full speed!

381
00:20:41,840 --> 00:20:43,900
S-senpai!

382
00:20:44,900 --> 00:21:06,120
Eeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeee!

383
00:21:06,120 --> 00:21:13,720
It's sinking fast! If we don't drop it, we'll die!
No way, I absolutely won't give up the gold for anything!

384
00:21:13,720 --> 00:21:14,440
I'm taking it home!

385
00:21:22,540 --> 00:21:25,620
Hey, that persistent guy is back!

386
00:21:25,620 --> 00:21:27,560
Eeeeeeh!

387
00:22:07,200 --> 00:22:08,160
Senpai

388
00:22:08,160 --> 00:22:08,940
Ryo-chan

389
00:22:08,940 --> 00:22:12,980
Umi-Gorilla-kun blew himself up!

390
00:22:16,700 --> 00:22:18,220
N-no way

391
00:22:18,220 --> 00:22:19,280
Ryo-chan

392
00:22:29,300 --> 00:22:30,120
Ryo-chan

393
00:22:30,120 --> 00:22:31,220
S-senpai

394
00:22:31,580 --> 00:22:32,980
Ow ow ow!

395
00:22:32,980 --> 00:22:33,740
So you're safe after all.

396
00:22:34,160 --> 00:22:35,180
Of course I am.

397
00:22:35,180 --> 00:22:37,500
Thank goodness. I was worried sick.

398
00:22:37,500 --> 00:22:40,540
I just got my hands on some treasure.
I'm not dying down here now.

399
00:22:40,540 --> 00:22:41,860
Then the gold bars too?

400
00:22:42,480 --> 00:22:45,780
It might not add up to 20 billion,
but grab as much as you can carry.

401
00:22:46,260 --> 00:22:47,740
I-I can't believe it.

402
00:22:49,280 --> 00:22:59,540
It's a miracle! Hey, hey, don't take it without permission! I risked my life to get this gold!
I can't take it all, since I'd die carrying it, so that's enough. Now, shall we head back?

403
00:22:59,540 --> 00:23:04,500
This time it's a happy ending Well,
now I'm a rich man too!

404
00:23:07,420 --> 00:23:11,460
You mean the whole seabed was fake?

405
00:23:12,460 --> 00:23:15,860
Yes, it was just a fabricated set,
painted gold.

406
00:23:15,860 --> 00:23:16,746
A few years ago,

407
00:23:16,796 --> 00:23:20,700
a ship used for a movie location
shoot apparently sank near there.

408
00:23:21,120 --> 00:23:24,740
The gold bars and the skeletons
were all props from that film.

409
00:23:25,720 --> 00:23:28,120
No way! Then what about all my hard work?!

410
00:23:28,800 --> 00:23:30,480
Trouble, Gorilla-kun!

411
00:23:30,680 --> 00:23:32,480
What now, Professor Tondemo!

412
00:23:32,860 --> 00:23:36,040
This! The Seabed Primitive
Man has been discovered!

413
00:23:36,660 --> 00:23:40,400
Let's head back out to
sea and capture it alive!

414
00:23:40,400 --> 00:23:44,200
Now, Professor Ezaki,
no matter how you look at it,

415
00:23:44,200 --> 00:23:45,600
isn't that just Ryo-chan?

416
00:23:46,700 --> 00:23:48,678
So, Professor Tondemo,

417
00:23:48,728 --> 00:23:52,560
I am in an incredibly bad mood right now.

418
00:23:53,320 --> 00:23:55,940
Never again will I go to the sea!

419
00:23:56,620 --> 00:23:58,800
Nooo! Dotto!

420
00:24:10,640 --> 00:24:14,740
In the gently passing seasons,

421
00:24:15,820 --> 00:24:19,540
I've gotten good at forced smiles.

422
00:24:20,740 --> 00:24:24,880
Swept along and changing, I am,

423
00:24:25,740 --> 00:24:29,260
how do I look in your eyes?

424
00:24:30,900 --> 00:24:36,140
After every fight,
we always share a brief kiss.

425
00:24:36,140 --> 00:24:40,200
You with your teary eyes, I loved you.

426
00:24:40,200 --> 00:24:45,420
Such irreplaceable things,

427
00:24:45,420 --> 00:24:50,940
how many of them does a
person ever hold in a lifetime?

428
00:24:52,680 --> 00:24:57,260
You are me, and I am you.

429
00:24:58,140 --> 00:25:02,280
That alone was enough to fill me up.

430
00:25:03,660 --> 00:25:08,480
Just by you smiling, look,

431
00:25:08,480 --> 00:25:15,040
it felt like every pain was healed.

432
00:25:22,120 --> 00:25:24,260
Who was Matsukichi again? You?

433
00:25:24,260 --> 00:25:27,520
That's cold, Ryo-san.
You don't even remember me?

434
00:25:27,520 --> 00:25:29,600
You're that delinquent kid from back then.

435
00:25:29,600 --> 00:25:32,040
And now you're a proper young entrepreneur

436
00:25:32,280 --> 00:25:33,920
No matter how I look at you,
you don't seem like one.

437
00:25:33,920 --> 00:25:36,100
Next time: Work hard, Masukichi!

438
00:25:36,100 --> 00:25:37,000
See you around.

